      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The focus on individual endangered species under managed conservation is a narrow, reactive triage that treats symptoms rather than curing the systemic disease. While invasive species are a threat, the long-term solution isn't constant human policing, but restoring the ecological complexity that naturally resists invasion. Rewilding addresses the root cause—habitat degradation and simplified ecosystems—thereby creating environments robust enough to support species naturally, without perpetual human babysitting.",
      "source": "target",
